From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:25:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(chunks): read counted border blocks before block entities

The LevelChunk tail after the biome palettes starts with an unsigned
border-block column count, followed by one packed X/Z byte per column,
then block entity NBT. The reader skipped only the count byte and parsed
the column bytes as NBT. Captured protocol-2225 Lifeboat Skyblock chunks
carry counts of 1 and 16; the old reader logged 16 "Error reading chunk
data" warnings per island load and silently stopped on 19 more columns.
Skip the counted bytes. A short list still ends the column through the
existing out-of-bounds path.

PowerNukkitX writes the same framing, capping the count at 255:
https://github.com/PowerNukkitX/PowerNukkitX/blob/93b06b1d7e3df0ea639f2164ec16205668d8faf8/src/main/java/org/powernukkitx/level/format/leveldb/LevelDBProvider.java
This change only consumes the border columns. It does not implement
border block behavior.

Upstream #466 now reads modern biome palettes across the full dimension
height. Keep packet regressions for zero, one and nine block sections,
both cache paths, repeated palettes and the trailing chest block entity.
Reading only the block section count shifts biome bytes into block entity
NBT and corrupts the resulting state.

The biome fixture reproduces errors from BDS 1.26.51.1 (protocol 2193).
The Dragonfly v0.11.5 network decoder also reads the full dimension range:
https://github.com/df-mc/dragonfly/blob/v0.11.5/server/world/chunk/decode.go

Border cases cover counts 1, 16 and 200 before a valid block entity, a
coordinate byte equal to the compound tag ID, and a truncated list.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/WorldPackets.java b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/WorldPackets.java
index afcc1205ddfa8a749be4d1e58fd62e8320cab262..949e0818376bff6ed57fc74a3aae2aab9ee87400 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/WorldPackets.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/WorldPackets.java
@@ -279,6 +279,7 @@ public final class WorldPackets {
                                 section.addPalette(PaletteType.BIOMES, new BedrockBiomeArray(biomeData));
                             }
                         } else {
+                            // Biomes cover the dimension height, independently of the block section count.
                             for (int i = 0; i < sections.length; i++) {
                                 BedrockDataPalette biomePalette = BedrockTypes.RUNTIME_DATA_PALETTE.read(dataBuf); // biome palette
                                 if (biomePalette == null) {
@@ -291,7 +292,8 @@ public final class WorldPackets {
                             }
                         }
 
-                        dataBuf.skipBytes(1); // border blocks
+                        // Border blocks: an unsigned column count, then one packed X/Z byte per column.
+                        dataBuf.skipBytes(dataBuf.readUnsignedByte()); // border block columns
                         while (dataBuf.isReadable()) {
                             final Tag tag = BedrockTypes.NETWORK_TAG.read(dataBuf); // block entity tag
                             if (tag instanceof CompoundTag) { // Ignore non-compound tags
diff --git a/src/test/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/LevelChunkBiomePacketTest.java b/src/test/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/LevelChunkBiomePacketTest.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9f4044de831ee9074f7cbe25ab59d95c795125b4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/test/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/LevelChunkBiomePacketTest.java
@@ -0,0 +1,171 @@
+/*
